To bring an existing hand‑made bucket into the kit’s `s3-bucket` module without recreating it, add the bucket to the module in `brownfield/adopt/main.tf` and attach it with an import block that points to the module’s resource.  
```hcl
module "reports_bucket" {
  source = "../../modules/s3-bucket"
  name   = "acme-legacy-reports"
  tags   = module.tags.tags
}

import {
  to = module.reports_bucket.aws_s3_bucket.this
  id = "acme-legacy-reports"
}
```

This function returns the path from the unit to the root `root.hcl`, producing unique keys such as `prod/us-east-1/network/tofu.tfstate` for each unit.  
```hcl
remote_state {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "my-tofu-state"
    key    = "${path_relative_to_include()}/tofu.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

